# =============================================================================
# motion-blocks — what stays out of git
# =============================================================================

# Dependencies — reinstall with `npm ci` (never committed)
node_modules/

# Render outputs — generated, never committed
out/
dist/
*.mp4
*.mov

# Remotion bundle dirs (rebuilt on every render; bundleToDir writes out/bundle-story)
out/bundle/
out/bundle-story/

# Large assets — synced separately, never in git
#   public/ (music, ~167M) — needed by the story pipeline (make_short.py),
#     not by the kit demos. Sync via shared drive, not git. A fresh clone
#     has NO public/music/, so make_short.py cannot build a soundtrack
#     (see README).
#   models/ (~338M, Kokoro TTS voice models) — same, synced separately.
#   references/ (~352M) — reference material, kept out entirely.
# Exception (2026-11-26): the two small fixture files in public/ ARE
# tracked — public/soundtrack.wav + public/kokoro-cues.json belong to the
# committed ice_floats story so a fresh clone can render with audio.
# The pattern below ignores everything else under public/ (incl. music/).
public/*
!public/soundtrack.wav
!public/kokoro-cues.json
!public/README.md
models/
references/

# Generated story data — built by scripts/make_short.py from stories/*.py.
# NOTE (cleanup 2026-11-26): the old .gitignore excluded
# src/story/currentStory.ts, which meant a fresh clone had NO story file
# and the bundle failed to build. The file is now TRACKED (the committed
# copy is the ice_floats story, 1742 frames) so the repo builds out of
# the box. make_short.py overwrites it on every story build — that is
# expected; do not hand-edit it.
# (No entry for it here on purpose.)

# Python — virtualenvs, bytecode, local tooling
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Logs and local state
*.log
render.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
